  "reason": "The strongest evidence is config_031: multimodal multiprofile with scvi_n200, ResNet50, avgpool, and weighted fusion achieved the best validation accuracy and F1. The main remaining uncertainty in this promising region is whether a stronger image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) can further improve performance, since PCA-based ViT was only marginally below PCA-based ResNet under the same aggregation and fusion. config_037 tests this by changing only the image encoder from ResNet50 to imagenet_vit_l while keeping the best-known RNA encoder, profile setting, aggregation, and fusion fixed. This is the best next use of budget because it exploits the current best direction with a single-factor extension, has high expected performance, and clarifies whether image encoder choice matters for the scvi_n200 multimodal design."
}

